Files: vibrantix-client-panel/src/components/grc/FrameworkComplianceMap.jsx — lines 937–942

Root Cause: The "Clear filters" button sets all four filter states to their defaults in one click:
```jsx
onClick={() => { setSearch(''); setStatusFilter('all'); setDomainFilter('all'); setAssetFilter('all'); }}
```
It does not save scrollYRef.current = window.scrollY before clearing. The useEffect on filteredDomains then fires and restores to whatever stale Y coordinate was saved from the previous filter interaction. For a user who has scrolled to domain 8, applied a filter (saving Y=1400), scrolled back to the top, and then cleared filters, the page jumps back to Y=1400 unexpectedly.

Claude Fix Prompt: In FrameworkComplianceMap.jsx, update the Clear filters onClick handler to save the scroll position first:
```jsx
onClick={() => {
  scrollYRef.current = window.scrollY;
  setSearch('');
  setStatusFilter('all');
  setDomainFilter('all');
  setAssetFilter('all');
}}
```
This is a one-line change consistent with how all other filter onChange handlers already save the scroll position.
